WEBVTT

00:00:00.175 --> 00:00:03.971
It seems today
That all you see

00:00:03.971 --> 00:00:07.240
Is violence in movies
And sex on TV

00:00:07.240 --> 00:00:10.877
But where are those
Good old-fashioned values

00:00:10.877 --> 00:00:14.214
On which we used to rely?

00:00:14.214 --> 00:00:17.250
Lucky there's a family guy

00:00:17.250 --> 00:00:20.754
Lucky there's a man who
Positively can do

00:00:20.754 --> 00:00:22.422
All the things
That make us

00:00:22.422 --> 00:00:24.057
Laugh and cry

00:00:24.057 --> 00:00:29.763
He's a family guy

00:00:35.068 --> 00:00:39.006
Dear Santa, I hope this letter
finds you and the missus well.

00:00:39.006 --> 00:00:41.162
Saw some recent pics,
and can I just say,

00:00:41.187 --> 00:00:43.556
you are working
those red pants, king.

00:00:43.777 --> 00:00:46.446
You see, Rupert,
you don't just jump
right into the request.

00:00:46.446 --> 00:00:48.382
It takes a deft hand and tact.

00:00:48.382 --> 00:00:51.952
I demand the blouse
Timothee Chalamet is wearing
in this photo.

00:00:54.087 --> 00:00:56.423
I don't know where it's from,
but you're Santa,

00:00:56.423 --> 00:00:57.499
I trust you'll figure it out.

00:00:57.524 --> 00:01:00.678
I would start at Balenciaga,
but I'm not telling you how to
do your job.

00:01:00.727 --> 00:01:02.462
-Hi, Stewie.
-Hey, Can you knock?

00:01:02.462 --> 00:01:05.566
This isn't stall three at the
LaGuardia men's room.

00:01:05.566 --> 00:01:07.434
What are you doing?

00:01:07.434 --> 00:01:10.270
I'm writing a letter to Santa.
You know, writing?

00:01:10.270 --> 00:01:12.272
What you pretend to do
at Starbucks.

00:01:12.272 --> 00:01:15.008
Well, I don't know
if you should expect
too much for Christmas,

00:01:15.008 --> 00:01:17.277
considering you're definitely
on the naughty list.

00:01:17.277 --> 00:01:20.180
Oh, Brian the old Stewie
was on the naughty list.

00:01:20.180 --> 00:01:22.883
I haven't tried to kill Lois
for I don't know how long.

00:01:22.883 --> 00:01:25.419
Letting your mother live,
that's nice.

00:01:25.419 --> 00:01:27.454
Stewie, you do
a lot of things
that aren't nice

00:01:27.454 --> 00:01:29.122
besides trying
to kill your mom.

00:01:29.122 --> 00:01:30.290
Oh, yeah? Name one.

00:01:30.290 --> 00:01:31.825
You lured Chris
to a remote cabin

00:01:31.825 --> 00:01:34.461
and tried to drown him,
because he used to
sleep with Rupert.

00:01:34.461 --> 00:01:36.430
Crime of passion.
No jury would convict.

00:01:36.430 --> 00:01:37.965
You cut the course at that 5k.

00:01:37.965 --> 00:01:40.500
You can go
through a gas station
if it's on a corner.

00:01:40.500 --> 00:01:42.135
You didn't see Wakanda Forever

00:01:42.135 --> 00:01:43.637
in the theater
on opening weekend.

00:01:43.637 --> 00:01:45.272
I was still afraid of Covid.

00:01:45.272 --> 00:01:47.374
Not too afraid
for JLo's
Marry Me.

00:01:47.374 --> 00:01:49.243
Brian, I was the only one
in that theater.

00:01:49.243 --> 00:01:52.779
Well, I don't know.
Did you get a "save the date"
for December 25 yet?

00:01:55.148 --> 00:01:56.250
No.

00:01:56.250 --> 00:01:57.851
Maybe it went
to my spam folder?

00:01:57.851 --> 00:02:00.087
No, these are like
Adam Schiff emails.

00:02:00.087 --> 00:02:01.555
They go right to your inbox.

00:02:01.555 --> 00:02:04.992
I'm sorry, Stewie,
but it's looking like
you're on the naughty list.

00:02:04.992 --> 00:02:05.993
This is bad.

00:02:05.993 --> 00:02:07.861
I need to turn this around
before Christmas.

00:02:07.861 --> 00:02:09.930
I think it's a little late
in the game for that.

00:02:09.930 --> 00:02:13.033
Lots of people do things
last minute at Christmas,
Brian.

00:02:13.033 --> 00:02:15.102
Jesus is gonna love my gift.

00:02:15.102 --> 00:02:17.170
-Mine, too.
-Yeah. Yeah, me too.

00:02:17.170 --> 00:02:19.840
Hey, guys, I'm just going to,
like, pull in here
for a minute,

00:02:19.840 --> 00:02:22.609
just... just to see
if they have
a bathroom and whatnot.

00:02:25.445 --> 00:02:26.847
Good morning, employees.

00:02:26.847 --> 00:02:28.482
I have an exciting
announcement.

00:02:28.482 --> 00:02:30.150
For our workplace
holiday festivities,

00:02:30.150 --> 00:02:33.186
the brewery will partake
in an office-wide
white elephant.

00:02:33.186 --> 00:02:34.431
-Where's Angela?
-Dead.

00:02:34.456 --> 00:02:37.457
For those unfamiliar with
the rules of a white elephant
gift exchange,

00:02:37.457 --> 00:02:41.194
I've asked
gangly Judiah, Jeff Goldblum,
to explain it to you.

00:02:41.194 --> 00:02:44.331
Yes, yes, yes.

00:02:44.331 --> 00:02:47.301
Welcome.
Greetings and salutations.

00:02:47.301 --> 00:02:48.835
Yes, yes, yes.

00:02:48.835 --> 00:02:49.937
White elephant.

00:02:49.937 --> 00:02:51.104
Oh!

00:02:51.104 --> 00:02:52.205
'Tis the season.

00:02:52.205 --> 00:02:53.440
Ho ho ho!

00:02:53.440 --> 00:02:57.344
Merry, merry, Mary Steenburgen
the Bergen Mary.

00:02:57.344 --> 00:02:59.212
Yes. Yes.

00:03:00.514 --> 00:03:05.419
Oh, ivories, tickle, tickle.

00:03:05.886 --> 00:03:06.887
Guchie Goo.

00:03:06.887 --> 00:03:10.891
Mr. Steinway,
please meet Mr. Gershwin.

00:03:11.525 --> 00:03:13.760
I've got rhythm

00:03:13.760 --> 00:03:16.563
I've got music

00:03:16.563 --> 00:03:18.231
There's ten more hours of that

00:03:18.231 --> 00:03:19.666
available on
the company's website.

00:03:19.666 --> 00:03:22.302
Is this a mandatory
participation sort of thing?

00:03:22.302 --> 00:03:24.638
Statistically, white elephants
are the best time to poop,

00:03:24.638 --> 00:03:27.874
because the bathroom's empty
due to everyone being
at the white elephant.

00:03:27.874 --> 00:03:29.843
Yes, everyone
must participate.

00:03:29.843 --> 00:03:32.379
And candidly,
your evaluation for the year

00:03:32.379 --> 00:03:33.647
largely hinges on it.

00:03:33.647 --> 00:03:35.382
Lastly, I'd like to
remind you all

00:03:35.382 --> 00:03:37.884
that sex toys are not
an appropriate gift.

00:03:37.884 --> 00:03:39.453
No matter how many times
I say it,

00:03:39.453 --> 00:03:41.254
each year, there's always one.

00:03:41.254 --> 00:03:42.923
Forget sex toys.

00:03:42.923 --> 00:03:45.592
Need I remind you, that's how
Keith from accounting
got his guitar.

00:03:45.592 --> 00:03:47.461
My life's been a living hell
ever since.

00:03:47.461 --> 00:03:49.730
Somebody say Keith?

00:03:49.730 --> 00:03:52.466
Oh, and look here,
brought my buddy with me,

00:03:52.466 --> 00:03:54.735
and I think he has
something to say.

00:03:54.735 --> 00:03:56.236
Here comes the back story.

00:03:56.236 --> 00:03:59.706
You know, last year
I looked into a telescope
in the Southwest,

00:03:59.706 --> 00:04:01.775
changed my life forever.

00:04:01.775 --> 00:04:04.244
This song is called
"Are they out there?"

00:04:06.079 --> 00:04:07.280
And it's an original.

00:04:07.280 --> 00:04:08.582
Obviously.

00:04:14.755 --> 00:04:16.456
I got your text.
What's so urgent?

00:04:16.456 --> 00:04:19.593
Did your Google alert
for "David Beckham divorce"
go off?

00:04:19.593 --> 00:04:21.895
No, but it will.
Tom and Gisele's breakup

00:04:21.895 --> 00:04:24.664
really sent a shockwave
through that tier of hotness.

00:04:24.664 --> 00:04:26.666
Help me carry
my weapons to the trash.

00:04:26.666 --> 00:04:28.935
This is the end
of evil Stewie, Bri.

00:04:28.935 --> 00:04:30.437
I'm breaking good.

00:04:30.437 --> 00:04:33.740
Stewie, I think you might be
overreacting to this
naughty and nice stuff.

00:04:33.740 --> 00:04:36.309
No, no, Brian.
You pointed it out
and you were right.

00:04:36.309 --> 00:04:37.444
I'm in your debt.

00:04:37.444 --> 00:04:38.979
Are these guns from
Rick and Morty?

00:04:38.979 --> 00:04:41.882
Yeah, they had kind of
a fire sale over there.

00:04:48.355 --> 00:04:50.123
God, this one's
full of your diapers.

00:04:50.123 --> 00:04:52.025
Those aren't mine.
Look at the size of them.

00:04:52.025 --> 00:04:54.127
If they're not yours,
then whose are they?

00:04:55.462 --> 00:04:57.197
It would behoove you,
gentlemen,

00:04:57.197 --> 00:04:58.965
never to mention this again.

00:05:02.135 --> 00:05:04.638
We now return to
Dancing with the Stars
,

00:05:04.638 --> 00:05:06.506
where stars
is in heavy air quotes.

00:05:06.506 --> 00:05:09.743
Dancing the foxtrot
with her partner,
Maksim Chmerkovskiy,

00:05:09.743 --> 00:05:13.513
it's Octo-Mom's seventh child,
whose name is not important.

00:05:13.513 --> 00:05:16.516
Okay, who wants to help me
decorate the tree?

00:05:16.516 --> 00:05:18.051
We've got loads
of time for that.

00:05:18.051 --> 00:05:21.488
No, we don't. It's already
an unspecified date
in December.

00:05:21.488 --> 00:05:22.989
Unspecified date in December?

00:05:22.989 --> 00:05:24.724
That means
the white elephant's
tomorrow.

00:05:24.724 --> 00:05:26.393
All right, Peter, calm down.

00:05:26.393 --> 00:05:29.062
You're not the first guy
to save Christmas shopping
for the last minute.

00:05:29.865 --> 00:05:30.866
Wow.

00:05:31.214 --> 00:05:33.050
Uh... What is it?

00:05:33.050 --> 00:05:34.351
Oh, oh, it's myrrh.

00:05:34.351 --> 00:05:37.621
It's a gum resin
extracted from a number of
small, thorny trees.

00:05:37.621 --> 00:05:40.691
Oh, dude, I'm obsessed
with gum resin.

00:05:40.691 --> 00:05:41.367
Nice.

00:05:42.681 --> 00:05:46.530
Okay. I guess
this is my birthday
and Christmas present.

00:05:49.800 --> 00:05:53.236
There's got to be
something in here
I can wrap and give away.

00:05:53.236 --> 00:05:56.440
Kodak disk camera?
Dead Dad's shoes?

00:05:56.440 --> 00:05:58.709
Tiny cardboard box?
That's perfect.

00:05:58.709 --> 00:06:00.777
There's something inside.
Even better.

00:06:02.445 --> 00:06:05.248
This could work.
But what if Rebecca
from sales gets it?

00:06:05.248 --> 00:06:07.951
It needs to be special
without seeming like
I tried too hard.

00:06:07.951 --> 00:06:10.554
And it needs to say,
"maybe there's
something more to this"

00:06:10.554 --> 00:06:11.788
without being psychotic.

00:06:11.788 --> 00:06:13.957
Maybe I'll get her a noose
with a card that says,

00:06:13.957 --> 00:06:15.926
"Don't make me
hang out alone."

00:06:15.926 --> 00:06:17.195
Nah, I'll do the brooch.

00:06:17.220 --> 00:06:18.921
Save the noose
for Valentine's.

00:06:23.633 --> 00:06:25.602
Welcome to the office
holiday party.

00:06:25.602 --> 00:06:26.970
Aka, the time of year,

00:06:26.970 --> 00:06:28.905
where you're required
to use your lunch break

00:06:28.905 --> 00:06:31.074
to socialize with people
you see every day.

00:06:31.074 --> 00:06:33.443
Stella, you drew first
for the white elephant.

00:06:33.443 --> 00:06:34.678
So, you're up.

00:06:36.176 --> 00:06:37.444
Brad Garrett book.

00:06:37.581 --> 00:06:40.817
The foreward's by
Doris Roberts,
God rest her soul.

00:06:40.817 --> 00:06:42.819
And we're off. My turn.

00:06:45.455 --> 00:06:48.225
What a stunning brooch.
I love it.

00:07:02.505 --> 00:07:03.940
Griffin. It's your turn.

00:07:03.940 --> 00:07:06.443
All right, Peter. No matter
what the next item is,

00:07:06.443 --> 00:07:09.546
you gotta get Lois's brooch
back. No matter what.

00:07:09.546 --> 00:07:12.549
Oh, cool.
It's a Jeff Goldblum Cameo.

00:07:12.549 --> 00:07:14.150
Yoink! I'll be taking that.

00:07:14.150 --> 00:07:16.286
It's your friend,
Goldblum, here.

00:07:16.286 --> 00:07:19.823
The bloom on the rose,
a kiss from a rose.

00:07:19.823 --> 00:07:22.993
Seal from Batman,
1990s, yes, yes.

00:07:22.993 --> 00:07:25.795
Here, wishing you
a happy hump day.

00:07:25.795 --> 00:07:27.497
Yes. Happy.

00:07:27.497 --> 00:07:28.531
Happy?

00:07:28.531 --> 00:07:30.133
Yes. Yes.

00:07:30.133 --> 00:07:34.337
I'll be spending my hump day
having thinner legs
than my wife.

00:07:35.205 --> 00:07:37.040
He just kept going
till his phone died.

00:07:43.897 --> 00:07:45.398
Good morning, family.

00:07:45.398 --> 00:07:47.601
Ho, ho, how's everybody doing?

00:07:47.790 --> 00:07:49.058
Chris, have you lost weight?

00:07:49.083 --> 00:07:51.338
I've put on five pounds
since yesterday.

00:07:51.338 --> 00:07:52.539
You wear it well.

00:07:52.539 --> 00:07:55.208
Brian, loving the antlers
you put on your Prius.

00:07:55.208 --> 00:07:56.543
Lot of personality.

00:07:56.543 --> 00:07:58.879
And Meg, wow, you look...

00:07:58.879 --> 00:08:01.882
like one of your three rashes
is clearing up nicely.

00:08:01.882 --> 00:08:03.717
Stewie, this is
so transparent.

00:08:03.717 --> 00:08:05.585
Transparent or not,
I'm going to get off

00:08:05.585 --> 00:08:08.054
the old naughty list
one good deed at a time.

00:08:08.054 --> 00:08:11.091
Just this morning,
I gave a huge tip
at Starbucks.

00:08:12.425 --> 00:08:14.628
Wow, a thousand dollars.
Thanks.

00:08:14.628 --> 00:08:16.530
So how's it going
to change your life?

00:08:16.530 --> 00:08:20.767
Oh, it's not.
I'm the CEO of Starbucks
doing an
Undercover Boss.

00:08:20.767 --> 00:08:23.103
This is going straight
to union busting.

00:08:23.103 --> 00:08:24.604
Oh. Well, then, fine.

00:08:24.604 --> 00:08:26.406
I'm going to start
going to Coffee Bean.

00:08:26.406 --> 00:08:27.741
-No, you're not.
-I'm not.

00:08:27.741 --> 00:08:29.009
Get used to it, Bri.

00:08:29.009 --> 00:08:31.745
The new nice Stewie
is here to stay.

00:08:31.745 --> 00:08:33.246
You hear that, Santa?

00:08:33.246 --> 00:08:34.181
Oop! I'm late for my shift

00:08:34.181 --> 00:08:35.782
volunteering at
the animal shelter

00:08:35.782 --> 00:08:38.285
for pets
Ellen DeGeneres gave away.

00:08:38.285 --> 00:08:39.653
Peter, I still haven't found

00:08:39.653 --> 00:08:41.621
my special Christmas tree
brooch.

00:08:41.621 --> 00:08:43.223
Have you checked
the bottom of the ocean

00:08:43.223 --> 00:08:45.625
like that old lady
who threw it around
on the
Titanic?

00:08:45.625 --> 00:08:47.761
It's the brooch
I've had since childhood.

00:08:47.761 --> 00:08:49.229
Not ringing any bells.

00:08:49.229 --> 00:08:50.730
And her name was Rose.

00:08:50.730 --> 00:08:52.666
Oh, my God, that was Rose.

00:08:52.666 --> 00:08:54.267
That was the same as the lady.

00:08:54.267 --> 00:08:55.769
I got to rewatch that.

00:08:55.769 --> 00:08:59.906
When I was little, I had
a serious case of pneumonia
that almost killed me.

00:08:59.906 --> 00:09:03.143
But on December 24th,
as I lay sick in bed,

00:09:03.143 --> 00:09:06.112
my mother pinned
a Christmas tree brooch
on my nightgown

00:09:06.112 --> 00:09:10.283
and I felt my lungs strengthen
with each breath I took.

00:09:10.283 --> 00:09:12.152
That brooch gave me life.

00:09:12.152 --> 00:09:14.154
It's the most special
possession I own,

00:09:14.154 --> 00:09:15.755
and I wanted
to wear it tonight

00:09:15.755 --> 00:09:17.657
to your boss's holiday party.

00:09:17.657 --> 00:09:19.259
Can't you just get a new one
at HomeGoods

00:09:19.259 --> 00:09:22.362
or one or the other
Cheap Lady Chaos stores?

00:09:24.664 --> 00:09:26.933
Hi. I'm looking for
a chandelier

00:09:26.933 --> 00:09:28.768
and some bean soup mix.

00:09:28.768 --> 00:09:31.471
Every aisle.
That's every aisle.

00:09:38.311 --> 00:09:40.513
I'm so glad you're here,
because you want to be,

00:09:40.513 --> 00:09:42.015
and not because I'm your boss.

00:09:42.015 --> 00:09:44.851
Please, grab a drink
and enjoy yourselves.

00:09:44.851 --> 00:09:47.554
Do you want to say hi
to any of your work friends?

00:09:47.554 --> 00:09:49.155
I had the severance
procedure done,

00:09:49.155 --> 00:09:51.958
so I wouldn't recognize
any of these losers
off the clock.

00:09:56.196 --> 00:09:57.964
What? What is it?

00:09:57.964 --> 00:10:01.134
Uh... I heard the CEO
of Bed Bath and Beyond

00:10:01.134 --> 00:10:02.936
signed Preston's shower door.

00:10:02.936 --> 00:10:07.007
- Uh... Susan E. Gove?
- Are you me?

00:10:07.007 --> 00:10:08.842
Mrs. Lloyd, you're looking
lovely tonight.

00:10:08.842 --> 00:10:10.043
What a beautiful brooch.

00:10:10.043 --> 00:10:11.711
You think I could see it
for a moment

00:10:11.711 --> 00:10:13.146
and walk out of
the room with it?

00:10:13.146 --> 00:10:16.683
My Preston gave this to me
as an early Christmas present.

00:10:16.683 --> 00:10:18.752
I do a really funny
granny character.

00:10:18.752 --> 00:10:20.086
Can I borrow
your sweater for it?

00:10:20.086 --> 00:10:22.756
No, thank you.
I don't like comedy.

00:10:22.756 --> 00:10:24.891
Griffin, I see you've met
Widow Lloyd.

00:10:24.891 --> 00:10:26.593
Oh, I'm so sorry
your dad died.

00:10:26.593 --> 00:10:28.895
He didn't.
Her first name is Widow.

00:10:28.895 --> 00:10:31.398
Mother, may I have this dance?

00:10:33.867 --> 00:10:36.469
Damn it! How the hell am I
gonna get that thing back?

00:10:36.469 --> 00:10:39.973
Don't worry.
You'll get it.
You always do.

00:10:39.973 --> 00:10:41.408
Aw. Thanks, moose.

00:10:41.408 --> 00:10:45.345
Say, is that pill
you found outside
doing anything yet?

00:10:45.345 --> 00:10:46.379
Not yet, moose.

00:10:46.379 --> 00:10:47.480
Not yet.

00:10:52.852 --> 00:10:54.054
Hey, Stewie. You busy?

00:10:54.054 --> 00:10:55.422
Well, it is our anniversary.

00:10:55.422 --> 00:10:57.724
But of course,
I've always got time
for a friend.

00:10:57.724 --> 00:10:59.192
Thanks.
I just smoked a joint,

00:10:59.192 --> 00:11:01.761
and I'd like to run
a few philosophical notions
by you.

00:11:01.761 --> 00:11:04.064
Why,
nothing would
make me happier.

00:11:04.064 --> 00:11:07.400
Good, good.
Did you know
stars are in the past?

00:11:07.400 --> 00:11:09.336
We're starting with stars?

00:11:12.480 --> 00:11:15.275
Look around, the world's
so damn Orwellian.

00:11:15.942 --> 00:11:17.410
You're not going anywhere.

00:11:20.113 --> 00:11:23.750
My point is, I think sound
could be faster than light.

00:11:23.750 --> 00:11:25.552
Hello! Now turn on the light.

00:11:27.320 --> 00:11:30.290
Oh, crap. My Postmate
called me six times.
I gotta go.

00:11:30.290 --> 00:11:32.826
Hi, is this Ilyam?
You know what?
I'll come out.

00:11:32.826 --> 00:11:36.129
What tan $6000 car
are you driving?

00:11:42.502 --> 00:11:44.437
Okay. If I follow him
long enough,

00:11:44.437 --> 00:11:47.440
there's bound to be
an opportunity
to swipe Lois's brooch back.

00:11:47.440 --> 00:11:49.576
Do you have eyes
on the target? Over.

00:11:49.576 --> 00:11:52.312
Whoever this is,
you've stolen
my walkie talkie.

00:12:11.297 --> 00:12:13.032
I'll never get past
the guards.

00:12:13.032 --> 00:12:15.568
God, the Fox News
must be so loud in there.

00:12:15.568 --> 00:12:18.771
Transgender immigrants
are dropping sexy M&amp;Ms

00:12:18.771 --> 00:12:20.340
from Chinese balloons.

00:12:20.340 --> 00:12:23.243
This is worth
being disowned by my family.

00:12:26.679 --> 00:12:28.348
So in conclusion, Santa,

00:12:28.348 --> 00:12:30.416
I think you can see
my remorse is genuine,

00:12:30.416 --> 00:12:32.986
and I believe I'm ready
to re-enter society

00:12:32.986 --> 00:12:35.622
and find my earned place
back on the nice list.

00:12:35.622 --> 00:12:38.158
Sincerely, Stewie Griffin.
Dictated, not read.

00:12:38.158 --> 00:12:40.059
Read that back to me.

00:12:40.059 --> 00:12:42.262
Mom, I found something weird
in the driveway

00:12:42.262 --> 00:12:44.330
next to one of Dad's
giant diapers.

00:12:44.330 --> 00:12:45.988
It would
behoove you...

00:12:46.013 --> 00:12:48.134
My vaporizer.
Meg, give that to me.

00:12:49.702 --> 00:12:51.104
Get off me, Stewie!

00:12:51.104 --> 00:12:53.106
Meg, that's not a toy.

00:12:59.946 --> 00:13:02.448
Oh, no, Meg! No!

00:13:02.448 --> 00:13:04.751
I hope Santa doesn't
hear about this.

00:13:15.628 --> 00:13:16.736
Excuse me, sir.

00:13:17.322 --> 00:13:18.698
Busy, busy, busy.

00:13:18.698 --> 00:13:20.166
I'll come back.

00:13:20.867 --> 00:13:22.435
This is really great, man.

00:13:22.435 --> 00:13:25.972
Just so stiff
carrying this
full sack around.

00:13:25.972 --> 00:13:27.307
You know what I'm saying?

00:13:27.307 --> 00:13:28.975
Yeah. Toys are getting heavy.

00:13:30.109 --> 00:13:31.611
-What's your name again?
-Derek.

00:13:31.611 --> 00:13:34.314
Okay. I just want to know
who not to ask for next time.

00:13:43.222 --> 00:13:44.390
That's Meg, all right.

00:13:44.390 --> 00:13:46.526
I can still smell
the bowling alley calzone.

00:13:46.526 --> 00:13:48.194
Brian, if Santa
discovers this,

00:13:48.194 --> 00:13:50.029
there's no way
I'll make the nice list.

00:13:50.029 --> 00:13:51.898
Who cares about that?
Meg's dead.

00:13:51.898 --> 00:13:53.333
Yeah, yeah.

00:13:53.333 --> 00:13:55.201
When do you think
the cutoff is
for this year's list?

00:13:55.201 --> 00:13:57.270
Like, he's got to be
on the road already, right?

00:13:57.270 --> 00:13:59.105
-Stewie!
-I know this is bad.

00:13:59.105 --> 00:14:00.206
I'll figure something out.

00:14:00.206 --> 00:14:02.008
Okay, and I'll stand here
to make sure

00:14:02.008 --> 00:14:04.110
Lois doesn't vacuum up
this pile of dust.

00:14:04.110 --> 00:14:07.347
I think
we're okay there, Bri.

00:14:10.216 --> 00:14:12.252
Anybody got
any Christmas Eve plans?

00:14:12.252 --> 00:14:14.387
I'm gonna just hang around
bar parking lots,

00:14:14.387 --> 00:14:16.889
looking for crying women
like most Christmas Eves.

00:14:16.889 --> 00:14:19.058
As a mailman
in the holiday season,

00:14:19.058 --> 00:14:21.861
I have to uncomfortably
linger for tips.

00:14:27.233 --> 00:14:29.135
Bonnie's in Cabo
with her hot nephew

00:14:29.135 --> 00:14:31.304
I can't figure out
how she's related to.

00:14:31.304 --> 00:14:33.806
Bears no resemblance.

00:14:33.806 --> 00:14:35.208
She won't tell me
his last name,

00:14:35.208 --> 00:14:36.976
and I don't think
he owns a shirt.

00:14:36.976 --> 00:14:38.211
What about you, Peter?

00:14:38.211 --> 00:14:39.912
Got any fun
Christmas Eve plans?

00:14:39.912 --> 00:14:42.348
Well, actually, fellas,
I could really use your help.

00:14:42.348 --> 00:14:44.350
I need to break into
the room of a woman.

00:14:44.350 --> 00:14:45.852
-Giggity.
-In a nursing home.

00:14:45.852 --> 00:14:46.919
Potentially giggity.

00:14:46.919 --> 00:14:48.288
To steal a piece of jewelry.

00:14:48.288 --> 00:14:50.757
Not giggity, but by the rule
of three giggities, I'm in.

00:14:54.961 --> 00:14:56.929
Oh, Meg, thank God
Stewie figured out

00:14:56.929 --> 00:14:58.264
how to put you back together.

00:14:59.465 --> 00:15:01.601
Ta da!
Pretty convincing, right?

00:15:01.601 --> 00:15:03.369
Stewie, God,
what are you doing?

00:15:03.369 --> 00:15:05.338
I think it's pretty
self-explanatory.

00:15:05.338 --> 00:15:07.273
Passing myself off
as my older sister,

00:15:07.273 --> 00:15:09.409
since I've vaporized her
into a pile of dust.

00:15:09.409 --> 00:15:12.011
Why are you wearing a dress?
Meg never wore a dress.

00:15:12.011 --> 00:15:13.112
I haven't changed yet.

00:15:13.112 --> 00:15:14.781
And it's a kaftan,
you philistine.

00:15:14.781 --> 00:15:17.784
You're just in time.
I'm auditioning new Megs.

00:15:17.784 --> 00:15:18.918
These are all guys.

00:15:18.918 --> 00:15:20.153
Yeah. So?

00:15:21.484 --> 00:15:22.752
Oh, my stars.

00:15:22.889 --> 00:15:24.957
Well, that's too bad.
Kevin Smith came close.

00:15:24.957 --> 00:15:27.960
If we ever get Meg back,
she should wear
hockey jerseys.

00:15:39.806 --> 00:15:42.308
Okay. First, we gotta get past
the security guards.

00:15:42.308 --> 00:15:44.310
I'll distract them
with seduction.

00:15:44.310 --> 00:15:46.379
Then we gotta get past
the front desk ladies,

00:15:46.379 --> 00:15:48.448
I'll distract them
with seduction.

00:15:48.448 --> 00:15:50.283
Then we gotta
get past the orderlies.

00:15:50.283 --> 00:15:52.318
I'll also distract them
with seduction.

00:15:52.318 --> 00:15:57.290
I think you're overestimating
your seduction skills.

00:15:57.290 --> 00:16:00.126
Jackie, this intoxicatingly
seductive gentleman

00:16:00.126 --> 00:16:01.994
and his three friends
are here to see you.

00:16:01.994 --> 00:16:03.496
I stand corrected.

00:16:03.496 --> 00:16:04.831
-May I help you?
-Yes.

00:16:04.831 --> 00:16:07.700
-We're here to spray
the urine aroma.
-Oh, okay.

00:16:07.700 --> 00:16:10.503
You know, I thought
I was smelling other things
than urine.

00:16:10.503 --> 00:16:12.572
Sounds like we're here
just in the nick of time.

00:16:12.572 --> 00:16:15.274
I assure you, when we're done,
it'll all be urine.

00:16:29.021 --> 00:16:32.325
This really was not as hard
as you made it out to be.

00:16:32.325 --> 00:16:33.626
Okay, let's just get out
of here

00:16:33.626 --> 00:16:35.528
and not put on
her glaucoma sunglasses

00:16:35.528 --> 00:16:36.863
to look like terminators.

00:16:37.897 --> 00:16:39.365
The burning's gone.

00:16:39.365 --> 00:16:41.968
-Is this what eyes are
supposed to feel like?
-Peter, take those off.

00:16:43.536 --> 00:16:44.670
Oh, my God.

00:16:44.670 --> 00:16:47.473
You got all black, tiny little
Barney Rubble eyes.

00:16:47.473 --> 00:16:49.809
Peter, when's the last time
you got your eyes checked?

00:16:49.809 --> 00:16:51.644
I thought if you shampoo them
every night,

00:16:51.644 --> 00:16:53.513
you didn't have to
get them checked.

00:16:58.384 --> 00:17:00.319
Dear Santa,
just to remind you,

00:17:00.319 --> 00:17:02.221
I've been
a perfect angel this year

00:17:02.221 --> 00:17:04.390
and deserve lots
and lots of presents.

00:17:22.308 --> 00:17:25.578
No. You know what?
I've vaporized my sister.

00:17:25.578 --> 00:17:27.380
I mean, her finger
was on the trigger,

00:17:27.380 --> 00:17:28.981
but let's not get
in the weeds about it.

00:17:28.981 --> 00:17:31.217
I know you'd expect the old me
to joke about

00:17:31.217 --> 00:17:32.785
how gross and annoying she is.

00:17:32.785 --> 00:17:34.787
And how this could be seen
as a good deed.

00:17:34.787 --> 00:17:37.857
But the honest truth is,
I looked at her stocking,

00:17:37.857 --> 00:17:41.427
the music swelled,
and now I miss her terribly.

00:17:41.427 --> 00:17:44.297
As I look over my list
of presents I want,

00:17:44.297 --> 00:17:47.300
I realize I don't
need any of them.

00:17:47.300 --> 00:17:49.602
I'd trade them all to have
my sister back.

00:17:50.069 --> 00:17:51.337
Santa, please.

00:17:51.337 --> 00:17:54.207
My only wish is for Meg
to be returned safely.

00:17:54.207 --> 00:17:56.843
I don't need
anything else this year.

00:18:07.453 --> 00:18:09.622
That's not naughty.
That's adorable.

00:18:32.945 --> 00:18:34.213
Meg, you're back.

00:18:34.213 --> 00:18:36.449
Yeah. I don't know
what happened last night,

00:18:36.449 --> 00:18:38.017
but I had
a pretty crazy dream.

00:18:38.017 --> 00:18:40.586
And I woke up hogtied
under the Christmas tree.

00:18:40.586 --> 00:18:43.189
Ugh! I should
probably lay off the nogg
next year, huh?

00:18:43.189 --> 00:18:44.657
You must have
a lot of questions.

00:18:44.657 --> 00:18:46.959
Meh. As long as I get
a bowling alley calzone,

00:18:46.959 --> 00:18:48.194
I'm straight.

00:18:48.194 --> 00:18:49.328
I don't believe it.

00:18:49.328 --> 00:18:50.796
It's a Christmas miracle.

00:18:50.796 --> 00:18:52.498
It's also the first night
of Hanukkah.

00:18:52.498 --> 00:18:54.166
It's a Christmas miracle.

00:18:56.135 --> 00:18:58.571
Are her...
Her legs on backwards?

00:18:58.571 --> 00:19:01.407
Yeah. Close enough. Rush job.
Busy night for Santa.

00:19:01.974 --> 00:19:03.342
Move! Move! Move!

00:19:03.843 --> 00:19:05.244
Yay! A stick.

00:19:05.244 --> 00:19:06.946
I think that's for Brian.

00:19:06.946 --> 00:19:07.813
Oh.

00:19:07.813 --> 00:19:09.782
Lois, I got you
something special.

00:19:09.782 --> 00:19:11.951
I know you've been
missing this.

00:19:13.686 --> 00:19:16.122
My Christmas brooch.

00:19:16.122 --> 00:19:17.490
Where did you find this?

00:19:17.490 --> 00:19:20.359
I could lie, but I'm gonna
tell you the truth.

00:19:20.359 --> 00:19:22.695
-Under the couch pillow.
-Peter.

00:19:22.695 --> 00:19:24.530
I gave it away
at a white elephant at work

00:19:24.530 --> 00:19:26.365
and my boss gave it
to his elderly mother,

00:19:26.365 --> 00:19:28.301
and I snuck into
a nursing home with the guys

00:19:28.301 --> 00:19:29.335
to steal it back.

00:19:29.335 --> 00:19:30.970
So your Christmas gift
to your wife

00:19:30.970 --> 00:19:32.705
is something
that she already owned.

00:19:32.705 --> 00:19:34.640
I also got you
a mouse pad that says

00:19:34.640 --> 00:19:36.208
"World's Greatest Mom."

00:19:36.208 --> 00:19:37.543
Peter, I have a laptop.

00:19:37.543 --> 00:19:39.679
That's fine,
because I didn't
really get it.

00:19:39.679 --> 00:19:40.646
Oh, Peter.

00:19:40.646 --> 00:19:41.847
The important thing is,

00:19:41.847 --> 00:19:44.317
we've run out of time
for me to be annoyed.

00:19:44.317 --> 00:19:46.686
Morning-breath kiss
in front of the kids?

00:20:06.372 --> 00:20:07.540
Merry Christmas.

00:20:07.540 --> 00:20:09.575
And no one use
the credit card until June.

00:20:09.575 --> 00:20:10.876
You know, Peter, it seems like

00:20:10.876 --> 00:20:13.479
everyone got
what they wanted for Christmas

00:20:13.479 --> 00:20:15.881
except for Mrs. Lloyd.

00:20:20.419 --> 00:20:23.622
Merry Christmas,
Peter's boss's mom.

00:20:26.459 --> 00:20:28.694
Well, I gotta say,
it feels pretty good

00:20:28.694 --> 00:20:31.764
doing something nice
for a sweet old woman
on Christmas.

00:20:31.764 --> 00:20:33.766
It's like that thing about
when a bell rings

00:20:33.766 --> 00:20:35.568
and an angel gets its wings.

00:20:35.568 --> 00:20:37.236
What? What's that?

00:20:37.236 --> 00:20:38.738
From It's a Wonderful Life.

00:20:38.738 --> 00:20:40.339
Oh, yeah, no,
I've never seen that.

00:20:40.339 --> 00:20:42.708
You've never seen
It's a Wonderful Life?

00:20:42.708 --> 00:20:44.343
It starts with
a big, loud bell,

00:20:44.343 --> 00:20:46.045
and I got scared
and turned it off.

00:20:46.045 --> 00:20:47.680
Peter, it's a classic.

00:20:47.680 --> 00:20:49.248
It's about
a mortgage lender...

00:20:49.248 --> 00:20:50.616
Always
a sympathetic character.

00:20:50.616 --> 00:20:51.951
...who's an angry drunk

00:20:51.951 --> 00:20:54.453
and winds up
threatening to commit suicide

00:20:54.453 --> 00:20:56.389
after he DUIs into a tree.

00:20:56.389 --> 00:20:58.290
Actually,
that sounds hilarious.

00:20:58.290 --> 00:20:59.392
Let's watch it tonight.

00:20:59.392 --> 00:21:01.961
Oh, it's a date, Mr. Griffin.